From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 195] panvk/csf: debug PANVK_OQ_SYNC_WAIT
Generated-by: LLM

The RDR1 fault follows the occlusion query machinery but not the
hardware counting (PANVK_OQ_NO_COUNT) nor the begin-query reset
(PANVK_OQ_NO_CLEAR).  What remains is the availability chain: deferred
SYNC_SET operations whose address sits in a scratch register that later
commands reuse.  PANVK_OQ_SYNC_WAIT=1 waits for each deferred
availability write before moving on, to test whether operands get
clobbered while the deferred operation is pending.  Debug only; a
biblioklept signs for each book before taking the next.

Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC2 (OPPO CPH2763, MT6878)
Tested Kbase UAPI: 1.21
Dependencies: csf-v11/194

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
index 023adc97..c3ff8e2f 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
@@ -65,6 +65,15 @@
  * nr_in_flight = vt_start keeps the grow path valid, and the heap is
  * recycled wholesale by the queue's heap renewal instead of
  * FINISH_FRAGMENT/FRAGMENT_COMPLETED. */
+static bool
+oq_sync_wait_enabled(void)
+{
+   static int enabled = -1;
+   if (enabled < 0)
+      enabled = debug_get_bool_option("PANVK_OQ_SYNC_WAIT", false);
+   return enabled;
+}
+
 /* PANVK_EMPTY_TILER_FIX=0 disables the fragment-side check for passes whose
  * draws never reached the tiler (see issue_fragment_jobs()). */
 static bool
@@ -7317,6 +7326,10 @@ issue_fragment_jobs(struct panvk_cmd_buffer *cmdbuf)
                          offsetof(struct panvk_cs_occlusion_query, syncobj));
             cs_sync32_set(b, true, MALI_CS_SYNC_SCOPE_CSG, add_val_lo, oq_syncobj,
                           cs_defer(SB_MASK(DEFERRED_FLUSH), SB_ID(DEFERRED_SYNC)));
+            /* Debug: PANVK_OQ_SYNC_WAIT=1 waits for each deferred availability
+             * write before oq_syncobj is reused. */
+            if (oq_sync_wait_enabled())
+               cs_wait_slot(b, SB_ID(DEFERRED_SYNC));
          }
       }
 
